# Super rally: simplified supplied Challenger (2026-11-09)

The owner supplied `Dodge Challenger HellCat - Rigged.blend`, requested its use after simplification, then requested completely opaque windows and removal of the interior. This replaces the earlier procedural C3 design. The public vehicle remains **Super rally**; its existing Rally-based handling, 198 km/h tune, saved identity, liveries and fitted-part selections remain.

- **CHH01 — Simplify and fit:** offline reduction of the supplied exterior, transfer of its dense surface normals, restrained native materials and conversion to immutable native meshes. Default production geometry is **22,894 triangles**, compared with **911,774** triangles in the original body and four wheels: **97.49% fewer**. The retained offline full tier is 41,766 triangles. These assembled counts include the game's round tyres, five-spoke rims, calipers and underside; fragile source wheel details are replaced. No runtime Blender, GLTF parsing, Rigacar, skeleton or animation is required.
- **CHH02 — Opaque windows; no interior:** all glazing uses fully opaque dark native material, alpha 1, with two-sided rendering. Boundary-preserving pane reduction, small overlaps behind the pillars and a low-poly opaque glazing backing close source junction gaps. Both source cabin-floor slabs are discarded. No seats, dashboard, steering wheel, interior trim, source rig, widgets, studio, cameras, lights, HDRI, packed photos or original material textures ship. A plain exterior underside remains beneath the car.
- **CHH03 — Game integration:** preserve canonical wheel contacts, use the supplied body/hood/spoiler/lamps, fit existing hood/aero/body/rim choices to the new envelope and update only Super rally's livery projection, wash height, headlamp mount and Garage detail-camera targets. Native paint remains per-car mutable; brake/night lighting, weathering, washing, ghosts and cached fitted modules retain existing behavior. Mesh inputs are explicitly routed to Super rally in the shared prepared-asset dependency manifest. Prepared bases, all car modules, Garage scenes and catalogue/menu/header/news pictures refresh coherently.
- **CHH04 — Credit and provenance:** Settings → Licences → Super rally car model credits Richerworld, the source, licence and modifications. Branding meshes and source textures are removed. The original downloaded `.blend` stays untouched.

