## Retained findings and limits

Initial reduction of the source wheel meshes deformed rims; final production uses the native round tyres and rims. Earlier source glazing reductions left narrow pillar gaps: the bright probe caught them. The final boundary-preserving panes and opaque backing pass the strict pixel check. Initial desktop Mobile comparisons included an unfinished showroom reveal and changed by a few 1-LSB pixels; the test now finishes all reveal/paint/kit transitions and verifies an exact repeat before introducing the probe. Pixel equality was not relaxed.

The first cached-part comparison had eight failures caused by absent UV data on imported surfaces versus zero UVs in batched assemblies. Explicit neutral UVs/white colours fix the import; the unchanged comparison then passes. The dependency audit also identified that the new mesh root needed an explicit consumed-input rule; the final refresh includes it. An intermediate native bake encountered a transient concurrent `condition_store.gd` constant parse error; later clean runs retain the other author's current file.

The existing broad Licences-page test reports **545 checks / 1 failure**: Kart credit bytes contain CRLF while `RichTextLabel` renders LF. The unchanged task-start Kart entry reproduces this discrepancy; the exact text after CR removal matches. Its original assertion and source file are retained. The new Challenger notice uses LF and renders byte-exactly, including source, artist and licence URL. [Diagnostic](evidence/challenger-hellcat-2026-11-09/licence-diagnostic.json). Sandbox certificate-store diagnostics remain in engine logs; test backend configuration is explicitly offline.

The [16-file source-only checkpoint](evidence/challenger-hellcat-2026-11-09/source-only.patch) passes `git apply --check --reverse`. The [source/resource receipt](evidence/challenger-hellcat-2026-11-09/source-receipt.json) records 18 byte-exact canonical controls and all 34 native resource/manifest hashes; the original model remains byte-exact. The physics test's single changed livery assertion was reconstructed for its baseline because that test was omitted from the initial snapshot; the limitation is explicit in its receipt. Generated scenes, binaries, metadata, documentation and unrelated concurrent work are excluded from the source patch.

No device query/test, APK export/install, owner-save/process change, live/backend request, deployment or main-index staging/commit was performed. Restart/reload and owner appearance acceptance remain; Android appearance, frame time, memory and thermal behavior are unqualified.

